rewrite:
The parties agree that certain events will trigger a "Release Condition" under the Escrow Agreement. These events include: 

Ehave going bankrupt or being unable to pay its debts; 
Ehave being forced into bankruptcy or insolvency by a court; 
Ehave applying for or agreeing to a receiver or trustee being appointed for it or its property; 
Ehave being forced to have a receiver or trustee appointed for it or its property; 
Ehave consenting to a bankruptcy petition being filed against it; 
A bankruptcy petition being filed against Ehave and not being dismissed within 60 days; 
Ehave being declared bankrupt or insolvent by a court; 
Ehave admitting it can't pay its debts as they become due; 
Ehave stopping its business as usual; 
Ehave changing ownership or being part of a merger or takeover; 
Ehave taking steps to dissolve or shut down; 
Ehave stopping its provision of the Ehave Companion Solution or support services for 15 business days or more, unless this Agreement is being ended by Ehave in accordance with its terms.

